WEBVTT

﻿1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.080
Did you kill your wife. Michael?
No. I did not.

2
00:00:03.080 --> 00:00:07.040
Stay with us. just for tonight.
No. I need to be here for Dad.

3
00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:09.840
The Governors are all agreed.
A suspension is a pause.

4
00:00:09.840 --> 00:00:11.760
There needn't be
any negative connotation.

5
00:00:11.760 --> 00:00:14.480
I know you'll have looked
through her phone records

6
00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:15.720
and seen how much we spoke.

7
00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:18.000
'His name is Stephen Sedgwick.
He's a dad at the school.'

8
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.560
He was having an affair with Sarah.

9
00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:22.600
Dylan's dad's been arrested. sir...
for murder.

10
00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.320
This case you're working on
at the school.

11
00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.360
it does still mean
you'll be working on Tina?

12
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:28.360
What did I promise you in 2004?

13
00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:29.840
You'd find the bastard who did it.

14
00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:33.480
What have you got in your pocket?
Diary pages. from Mum's Filofax.

15
00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:36.280
What are you gonna do about them?
Burn them.

16
00:00:38.000 --> 00:00:44.074
Press play. Subtitles appear.
200+ languages. One app:  tryray.app

17
00:01:36.560 --> 00:01:38.440
At least we still have each other.

18
00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:41.400
Right?

19
00:01:46.039 --> 00:01:49.000
I'm gonna go to Nan and Grandad's.
just for a few nights.

20
00:01:49.000 --> 00:01:50.039
make sure they're OK.

21
00:01:56.479 --> 00:01:58.360
Yeah. That's a good idea.

22
00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:17.440
He knew about the affair.
makes this big song and dance

23
00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:20.000
about not knowing anything.
but he knew about the affair.

24
00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.520
Yeah. He's gone round
to do something about it.

25
00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:24.040
He's clearly agitated. in't he?

26
00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:26.560
Mm.
Don't you think?

27
00:02:29.760 --> 00:02:32.640
If he lied to us about the affair.
what else has he lied about?

28
00:02:37.400 --> 00:02:40.160
Well. there's a chance that
Sarah might not have been killed

29
00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:41.760
until as late as the Thursday.

30
00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:45.320
So. the rugby match didn't help him.
No.

31
00:02:45.320 --> 00:02:48.160
Which means his alibi's gone.
Which means his alibi's gone.

32
00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:50.680
We need to bring him in
and see what else he's hiding.

33
00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:53.000
Where's Ivan?

34
00:02:53.000 --> 00:02:54.920
Calling CPS
so we can charge Stephen Sedgwick.

35
00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:55.960
Yes. but where?

36
00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:57.760
We've got plenty of corroboration.

37
00:02:57.760 --> 00:03:01.000
and the forensics'll be
at the cottage first thing.

38
00:03:01.000 --> 00:03:03.200
I mean. I know we don't judge a book
by its cover. but...

39
00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.800
Wait! Samira.
can I just call you back? OK.

40
00:03:44.520 --> 00:03:46.920
I want you to know.
whatever happens.

41
00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:49.160
this is a safe place.

42
00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:51.400
Erm. what do you mean?

43
00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.640
It means you can come here.
shut everything away.

44
00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:56.600
Everyone needs a place like that.
don't they?

45
00:03:56.600 --> 00:03:59.040
Sorry. what do you...?
What do you mean. "safe"?

46
00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:01.280
Oh. it's just...

47
00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:03.120
it's just what your mum
used to call it.

48
00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:06.280
She used to call it her safe place.

49
00:04:08.720 --> 00:04:11.800
OK. right. I'm gonna leave
the landing light on.

50
00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.880
just so you don't wake up
and forget where you are.

51
00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:16.560
OK?
Yeah.

52
00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:45.320
ALARM BEEPING

53
00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.240
BEEPING STOPS

54
00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:06.720
DOORBELL RINGS

55
00:05:19.160 --> 00:05:20.600
Michael Polly. I'm arresting you

56
00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:22.920
on suspicion of the murder
of Sarah Polly.

57
00:05:26.160 --> 00:05:28.480
Michael Polly has been suspended.

58
00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:31.000
and Alana Polly
is still on compassionate leave.

59
00:05:32.000 --> 00:05:34.760
The other update
is that the police are wanting

60
00:05:34.760 --> 00:05:36.520
to talk to you all individually.

61
00:05:36.520 --> 00:05:38.159
MURMURING

62
00:05:38.159 --> 00:05:41.720
I've said I'm sure that won't be
a problem for any of us. given...

63
00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:45.880
HE SIGHS

64
00:05:45.880 --> 00:05:48.200
..well. given what's happened.

65
00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:51.280
The message is we are cooperating
in every way possible

66
00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:53.880
while continuing with the timetable.
Yes.

67
00:05:53.880 --> 00:05:56.600
ALL CHATTER

68
00:05:56.600 --> 00:05:58.480
Can we...? Can we all please...?
Let's just...

69
00:05:58.480 --> 00:06:02.400
Let's please try not to take this
back to our respective classrooms.

70
00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:04.800
All right. thank you. everybody.

71
00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:10.520
My client would like to make
the following statement.

72
00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:14.160
While he has of course been willing
and happy

73
00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:15.680
to answer all of your questions.

74
00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:18.760
Mr Polly now believes he has stated.
more than once.

75
00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:20.800
that there is nothing
more substantial he can add.

76
00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:23.520
either in helping you find
the person responsible

77
00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:24.800
for the death of his wife

78
00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:27.520
or in terms of explaining
his own whereabouts and actions

79
00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:28.720
during that time.

80
00:06:30.040 --> 00:06:32.920
As such. he will not be answering
any more of your questions.

81
00:06:36.040 --> 00:06:37.440
Is that right. Michael?

82
00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:41.000
Why. when we asked you if there was
anything else we should know.

83
00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:43.680
did you fail to mention your wife's
affair with Stephen Sedgwick?

84
00:06:46.480 --> 00:06:50.880
Or the fact you visited his property
on the night she went missing...

85
00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:53.880
..and you chose not to tell us?

86
00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:56.440
Michael?

87
00:07:00.120 --> 00:07:02.280
Would you like me to read
the statement out again.

88
00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:03.960
or did you hear it the first time?

89
00:07:10.680 --> 00:07:13.400
He's definitely hiding something.
but that is not footage

90
00:07:13.400 --> 00:07:17.200
of a man committing a crime.
or even at a crime scene.

91
00:07:17.200 --> 00:07:20.680
or thinking about it. even anywhere
near the victim of the crime.

92
00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:22.960
To be honest.
I'm not sure it gives us anything.

93
00:07:22.960 --> 00:07:24.840
And Polly knows it.
It shows us he lied.

94
00:07:24.840 --> 00:07:26.880
It shows he gets angry. motive.
It's not evidence.

95
00:07:26.880 --> 00:07:29.320
No. but it helps. That's how
it works. We get there in stages.

96
00:07:29.320 --> 00:07:32.760
If it were me.
I'd be working that timeline.

97
00:07:32.760 --> 00:07:35.200
Where were Michael Polly
and Stephen Sedgwick

98
00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:37.440
during the three-day period

99
00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.440
between the last sighting
of Sarah Polly

100
00:07:39.440 --> 00:07:41.480
and her body being found?

101
00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:43.960
They are
our two most credible suspects.

102
00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:46.720
but we can't hold either of them
without more evidence.

103
00:07:48.120 --> 00:07:49.440
We have to release them.

104
00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:53.720
So. let's get surveillance
on Sedgwick's house as well.

105
00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:57.680
Boss.

106
00:07:59.480 --> 00:08:00.760
Look. I don't know if you know.

107
00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:03.200
but I was actually the first person
on this case originally.

108
00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:05.200
I'm just wondering
if there's any way I can go back

109
00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:06.920
to doing
more of that investigative work.

110
00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:08.160
You're the FLO.

111
00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:11.240
Alongside being the FLO.
That's the job you've been given.

112
00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:13.360
And I like it. I really...
So keep doing it. please.

113
00:08:13.360 --> 00:08:16.400
Let the team focus on Michael Polly
and Stephen Sedgwick.

114
00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:18.760
And don't go over Ivan's head.
I... I wo...

115
00:08:18.760 --> 00:08:21.240
No. That's the end
of the conversation.

116
00:08:29.320 --> 00:08:32.400
MUSIC: 'Nice To Each Other'
by Olivia Dean

117
00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.799
For Ivan -
and he's a decent enough guy.

118
00:08:34.799 --> 00:08:36.919
I've worked with him -
you're a threat.

119
00:08:36.919 --> 00:08:38.159
Oh. please.

120
00:08:38.159 --> 00:08:41.360
We have two good suspects. and
I feel like I can't be effective.

121
00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:44.400
Come on.

122
00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:45.760
You could be the person who solves

123
00:08:45.760 --> 00:08:48.200
two of Bristol's
highest profile cases.

124
00:08:48.200 --> 00:08:50.320
I don't feel like I'm solving
anything at the moment.

125
00:08:50.320 --> 00:08:52.840
Well. don't speak too soon.
SHE SIGHS

126
00:08:52.840 --> 00:08:56.720
I said I'd look into the Tina files.
and I did.

127
00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:59.600
There was a handbag found.
wasn't there? Yeah.

128
00:08:59.600 --> 00:09:02.200
Her handbag. not far from the club.

129
00:09:02.200 --> 00:09:05.280
Her silver bag.
Well. I have a mate in FRC.

130
00:09:05.280 --> 00:09:08.000
And he has offered to do
a forensic review.

131
00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:10.240
You would do that for me?

132
00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:12.280
Yeah.

133
00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:14.360
For Tina. And Carol.

134
00:09:14.360 --> 00:09:15.920
That's the Mum's name. isn't it?
Yeah.

135
00:09:15.920 --> 00:09:17.600
Yeah.
Thank you.

136
00:09:19.160 --> 00:09:20.760
I mean it. Thank you.

137
00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:23.280
# Nice to each other... #

138
00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:25.560
Here we go. Pasta for the lady.

139
00:09:25.560 --> 00:09:28.560
Thank you. And pizza for the tramp.

140
00:09:28.560 --> 00:09:30.160
SHE CHUCKLES
WAITER: Enjoy.

141
00:09:34.480 --> 00:09:36.720
I've been thinking
about this situation with Michael.

142
00:09:36.720 --> 00:09:39.160
Yeah?
Mm.

143
00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:42.480
If he's not saying anything.
then technically. as FLO.

144
00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:44.360
I've got the best job there is.
haven't I?

145
00:09:44.360 --> 00:09:47.000
I'm right in there
with the suspect.

146
00:09:48.040 --> 00:09:49.880
I could interview him.
Without him knowing?

147
00:09:49.880 --> 00:09:53.480
Yeah. That's what I mean. yeah.
You'd be brilliant at that.

148
00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:57.040
But be careful.
You don't know what he's capable of.

149
00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:22.280
DOORBELL RINGS

150
00:10:48.560 --> 00:10:52.240
Alana not here?
She's gone to her grandparents'.

151
00:10:53.680 --> 00:10:54.720
Hm.

152
00:10:56.640 --> 00:10:58.160
They'll be wanting
to look after her.

153
00:10:58.160 --> 00:11:00.240
Well. she wants to look after them.

154
00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:02.800
She's lost her mother.
but they've lost their daughter.

155
00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.320
so she wants to be there for them.

156
00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:06.680
That's the type of young woman
she is.

157
00:11:11.680 --> 00:11:15.080
Sedgwick's neighbour has
CCTV cameras on his house.

158
00:11:15.080 --> 00:11:17.160
That's how they knew you were there.
Michael.

159
00:11:17.160 --> 00:11:19.960
That's why they arrested you.
It's not like they had any choice.

160
00:11:19.960 --> 00:11:21.480
And for what it's worth...

161
00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:23.040
Milk?
Yes. please.

162
00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:24.160
And for what it's worth.

163
00:11:24.160 --> 00:11:26.640
even though I could see
how agitated you were.

164
00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:28.920
I thought you might've been
after him. not her.

165
00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:34.640
I wasn't after anyone.

166
00:11:37.280 --> 00:11:39.040
You can't say that. Michael.

167
00:11:43.280 --> 00:11:44.760
No.

168
00:11:50.200 --> 00:11:52.120
You can say you didn't hurt Sarah.

169
00:11:52.120 --> 00:11:55.160
and you can refuse to answer
any more questions.

170
00:11:55.160 --> 00:11:58.840
but you can't just shrug that off
like it's normal behaviour. Michael.

171
00:11:58.840 --> 00:12:01.040
prowling around somebody's house
like that

172
00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:02.680
in the middle of the night.
I'm sorry. no.

173
00:12:03.880 --> 00:12:07.480
He was having an affair with
my wife. and she'd gone missing.

174
00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:09.880
So I thought
that's where she might be.

175
00:12:09.880 --> 00:12:11.560
And that makes sense. but...

176
00:12:11.560 --> 00:12:14.440
Did you see me talk to anybody
when I was there. on this CCTV?

177
00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:16.040
You've seen it. yeah?
Yeah.

178
00:12:16.040 --> 00:12:20.800
So did you see me confront anyone
or knock on the door?

179
00:12:23.840 --> 00:12:25.400
Well. then.

180
00:12:27.320 --> 00:12:28.440
"Well. then."

181
00:12:30.200 --> 00:12:33.680
You say "well. then"
like that's all there is to it.

182
00:12:33.680 --> 00:12:35.080
That is all there is to it.

183
00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:36.840
So. why didn't you tell us
about this affair

184
00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:38.360
when we first met. Michael?

185
00:12:39.880 --> 00:12:43.360
You know. if you can sit there
and be so matter of fact about it...

186
00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:46.480
..why not be like that then?

187
00:12:47.640 --> 00:12:50.240
Because...
It obviously hurt you. Michael.

188
00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:52.920
I saw you crying.
That was not to do with the affair.

189
00:12:57.120 --> 00:12:58.760
That was because she was gone.

190
00:13:00.120 --> 00:13:01.960
I see.
That was not to do with the affair.

191
00:13:01.960 --> 00:13:03.280
I apologise. I'm sorry.

192
00:13:17.440 --> 00:13:19.680
But the question still stands.
Michael.

193
00:13:19.680 --> 00:13:21.520
Why didn't you tell us
about this affair?

194
00:13:24.480 --> 00:13:28.480
Because people don't expect that
of people like Sarah and I.

195
00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:32.080
You know. erm...
people in our position.

196
00:13:32.080 --> 00:13:33.720
It's not easy for anyone. is it?

197
00:13:34.960 --> 00:13:36.360
That's not good enough.

198
00:13:44.000 --> 00:13:45.920
Because I knew.
and I didn't want to know.

199
00:13:48.120 --> 00:13:49.600
And because...

200
00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:54.080
..it wasn't easy to talk about.
that's all.

201
00:13:56.280 --> 00:13:57.720
And it's easier now. is it?

202
00:13:58.840 --> 00:14:00.080
With me?

203
00:14:15.880 --> 00:14:19.920
Charlie-X-ray-655. suspect
has returned from the office. over.

204
00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:23.960
SIGHS

205
00:14:44.520 --> 00:14:45.800
STEPHEN
EXHALES DEEPLY

206
00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:55.360
FAINT VIDEO GAME
PLAYS

207
00:14:58.160 --> 00:14:59.680
CONSOLE BEEPS

208
00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:06.960
It's not true.

209
00:15:06.960 --> 00:15:08.920
I want you both
to hear that from me.

210
00:15:08.920 --> 00:15:10.480
What's not true?

211
00:15:10.480 --> 00:15:12.720
I think you both know
what I'm talking about.

212
00:15:13.720 --> 00:15:16.440
Why don't you tell us?
Don't talk to him like that.

213
00:15:16.440 --> 00:15:18.760
Like what?
In that voice.

214
00:15:18.760 --> 00:15:20.960
It's a perfectly normal question
to ask.

215
00:15:22.000 --> 00:15:23.240
What's not true?

216
00:15:23.240 --> 00:15:28.000
That there was something
between me and... Sarah Polly.

217
00:15:30.720 --> 00:15:33.560
It's all over socials...
that you killed her.

218
00:15:35.960 --> 00:15:37.520
It's all your fault.

219
00:15:37.520 --> 00:15:40.200
and it's literally
all being taken out on me.

220
00:15:46.320 --> 00:15:49.240
VIDEO GAME RESUMES

221
00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:58.160
STEPHEN CLEARS THROAT

222
00:16:07.080 --> 00:16:10.760
I had the meeting.
We agreed I'll take a week off work.

223
00:16:16.880 --> 00:16:18.240
HE EXHALES DEEPLY

224
00:16:27.680 --> 00:16:31.360
Whatever you might think of me.
or think I might've done...

225
00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:32.920
I know what you've done.

226
00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:34.680
Just let me say
what I have to say. Claire.

227
00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:37.640
and then you can speak.
and I won't interrupt you. OK?

228
00:16:37.640 --> 00:16:38.800
SHE SIGHS

229
00:16:42.200 --> 00:16:43.680
Whatever you might be thinking.

230
00:16:43.680 --> 00:16:47.320
let's try and both remember what's
the most important thing here.

231
00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:51.720
That's the kids.

232
00:16:51.720 --> 00:16:54.240
You said it yourself.

233
00:16:54.240 --> 00:16:56.520
Dylan's school work is suffering.
and...

234
00:16:57.760 --> 00:17:00.480
..Freya's tests are full-on. so...
Don't make this about the kids.

235
00:17:00.480 --> 00:17:04.839
I'm just trying to make
my point here. baby. and then...

236
00:17:04.839 --> 00:17:07.440
and then. like I said.
I'll be a good listener for you.

237
00:17:10.440 --> 00:17:12.800
So. the less arguing and stress
they feel...

238
00:17:14.760 --> 00:17:16.440
..the better chances they have.

239
00:17:17.640 --> 00:17:19.240
I know we both agree on that.

240
00:17:27.640 --> 00:17:30.200
The police are gonna ask you
to help confirm my where...

241
00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:32.960
No. I'm nearly done. Claire. please.
I'm so nearly done.

242
00:17:34.080 --> 00:17:36.120
You know I didn't kill her.

243
00:17:36.120 --> 00:17:39.320
The police are gonna ask you
to help confirm my whereabouts

244
00:17:39.320 --> 00:17:41.600
around the time
Sarah Polly went missing.

245
00:17:41.600 --> 00:17:43.160
If I wasn't at work.
then where was I?

246
00:17:45.200 --> 00:17:48.480
And the answer is I was here.
in here. watching TV with you.

247
00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:51.640
whatever we were watching.
one of your programmes.

248
00:17:51.640 --> 00:17:53.880
That's all you have to tell them.

249
00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:56.480
And then all this goes away.

250
00:17:58.160 --> 00:18:00.920
For Dylan and for Freya.

251
00:18:02.880 --> 00:18:04.040
OK?

252
00:18:06.680 --> 00:18:08.560
SIGHS.
CHUCKLES

253
00:18:08.560 --> 00:18:10.120
Before we have our proper chat. I...

254
00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:13.040
..I really need to grab a shower.

255
00:18:13.040 --> 00:18:16.160
These last few days have been hard.

256
00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:18.000
I just wanna wash them away. Erm...

257
00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:49.680
His son. Dylan.

258
00:18:49.680 --> 00:18:52.720
he's a special talent
when it comes to the rugby.

259
00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:55.080
I mean. he struggles elsewhere
academically. but...

260
00:18:56.800 --> 00:18:58.960
..he's a rare talent
on the rugby field.

261
00:18:58.960 --> 00:19:00.800
I mean.
I don't tell him that. obviously.

262
00:19:00.800 --> 00:19:05.960
That's how you coach players.
but. erm... he's a joy to watch.

263
00:19:11.320 --> 00:19:14.400
Erm... the fact that she chose
his father.

264
00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:17.640
or let his father choose her.
whichever way round it was...

265
00:19:18.680 --> 00:19:21.920
..is a betrayal of our marriage.
of course. but...

266
00:19:21.920 --> 00:19:24.720
the damage it inflicts
is on so much more.

267
00:19:24.720 --> 00:19:27.640
It's on my family. his family.
on the school. on its reputation.

268
00:19:27.640 --> 00:19:28.680
And this boy...

269
00:19:29.760 --> 00:19:33.360
..who can make so much of himself
playing rugby. who loves it so much.

270
00:19:33.360 --> 00:19:36.360
you know. he gets the worst of me.
because of what I know.

271
00:19:38.680 --> 00:19:42.160
When I should be the best coach.
the best teacher he has...

272
00:19:43.200 --> 00:19:47.120
..I end up taking it out on him...
because of her betrayal.

273
00:19:48.600 --> 00:19:51.120
You know. it's cruel.
it's vindictive.

274
00:19:51.120 --> 00:19:52.760
And I. erm...

275
00:19:54.640 --> 00:19:57.040
..well. I let myself down.
that's all.

276
00:20:04.520 --> 00:20:06.120
How did you let yourself down?

277
00:20:07.680 --> 00:20:11.200
In the weeks leading up
to her going missing. I...

278
00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:13.720
..I was angry.

279
00:20:15.200 --> 00:20:16.360
And...

280
00:20:18.600 --> 00:20:21.040
..I did things that
I will never forgive myself for.

281
00:20:36.520 --> 00:20:40.680
Did you notice anything unusual or
strange about Michael or Sarah Polly

282
00:20:40.680 --> 00:20:42.600
in the run-up to her disappearance?

283
00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:44.200
Anything at all?

284
00:20:44.200 --> 00:20:47.760
I'd see her going off on walks
on her own.

285
00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:51.320
Where she was going. I've no idea.
I just want the rumours to stop.

286
00:20:51.320 --> 00:20:54.320
What rumours are those?
That he... That he killed her.

287
00:20:54.320 --> 00:20:57.040
I've not heard that myself.

288
00:20:57.040 --> 00:20:58.320
Not only has it not sunk in.

289
00:20:58.320 --> 00:21:00.680
I just can't imagine a time
when it will ever have sunk in.

290
00:21:00.680 --> 00:21:04.000
Would you be happy for us to have
a look through your phone? Mm.

291
00:21:05.080 --> 00:21:06.440
If you wouldn't mind?
Sure.

292
00:21:06.440 --> 00:21:08.720
Would you hand over your phone
so we can take a quick look?

293
00:21:08.720 --> 00:21:10.360
I will need that back at some stage.

294
00:21:12.880 --> 00:21:15.240
What was your relationship
with Sarah like?

295
00:21:15.240 --> 00:21:17.920
She was friendly.
We got on perfectly well.

296
00:21:17.920 --> 00:21:21.000
She did the choir.
And then there was the book club.

297
00:21:21.000 --> 00:21:22.840
SCOFFS SOFTLY
There was no book club.

298
00:21:22.840 --> 00:21:24.960
I wasn't invited to that.

299
00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:27.360
We scrapped it because
we couldn't get enough people.

300
00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:29.440
Not enough good people. anyway.

301
00:21:29.440 --> 00:21:31.080
But. erm. that's fine.

302
00:21:31.080 --> 00:21:33.360
I think she wanted to escape.

303
00:21:33.360 --> 00:21:36.640
She was having an affair.
I saw her by the art room.

304
00:21:36.640 --> 00:21:39.640
And I would see her sometimes
when I saw Alana.

305
00:21:39.640 --> 00:21:43.040
You can feel it.
It's as if they want it to be him.

306
00:21:43.040 --> 00:21:45.240
You can see it
on some of their faces.

307
00:21:45.240 --> 00:21:46.560
But he called her.

308
00:21:46.560 --> 00:21:48.160
He...?
Michael.

309
00:21:48.160 --> 00:21:50.160
As soon as he knew she was missing.
he called her.

310
00:21:50.160 --> 00:21:52.680
I was dropped at the front door
as an eight-year-old.

311
00:21:52.680 --> 00:21:54.880
and I've barely been away.
so trust me when I tell you.

312
00:21:54.880 --> 00:21:57.080
it's better under his leadership
than it's ever been.

313
00:21:57.080 --> 00:21:59.760
Well. it hasn't got
the best reputation.

314
00:21:59.760 --> 00:22:01.400
Does that mean
I always agree with him?

315
00:22:01.400 --> 00:22:02.920
Some teachers refuse to work here.

316
00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:04.800
He had his fallouts
with the parents.

317
00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:08.560
Yes. Do I think he has it in him
to kill Sarah?

318
00:22:08.560 --> 00:22:09.880
Michael Polly...

319
00:22:12.560 --> 00:22:13.880
..is a wonderful man.

320
00:22:13.880 --> 00:22:16.160
But someone's got to have done it.
haven't they?

321
00:22:16.160 --> 00:22:17.680
I can only go on
what I know of the man.

322
00:22:17.680 --> 00:22:18.840
and so I'd have to say...

323
00:22:18.840 --> 00:22:20.760
No way.
..no.

324
00:22:20.760 --> 00:22:24.320
Even though I dislike him. I would
say the same for Stephen Sedgwick.

325
00:22:26.240 --> 00:22:27.360
Thank you for that.

326
00:22:28.920 --> 00:22:30.440
'That was not to do
with the affair.'

327
00:22:30.440 --> 00:22:31.680
'I apologise. I'm sorry.'

328
00:22:31.680 --> 00:22:33.600
'I was angry.

329
00:22:34.640 --> 00:22:38.760
'And I did things that
I will never forgive myself for.

330
00:22:38.760 --> 00:22:40.720
'That was not to do
with the affair.'

331
00:22:40.720 --> 00:22:43.520
'I apologise. I'm sorry.'
'I was angry.

332
00:22:44.680 --> 00:22:47.640
'And I did things that
I will never forgive myself for.'

333
00:22:47.640 --> 00:22:50.720
'It obviously hurt you. Michael.
I saw you crying.'

334
00:22:50.720 --> 00:22:52.520
'That was not to do
with the affair.'

335
00:22:52.520 --> 00:22:55.040
'But the question still stands.
Michael. Why didn't you...?'

336
00:22:55.040 --> 00:22:57.640
PHONE RINGS

337
00:23:02.520 --> 00:23:06.520
Wondered if you'd call.
'It's for me to call you. is it?'

338
00:23:06.520 --> 00:23:09.600
Right now it is.
'That's called playing hard to get.'

339
00:23:09.600 --> 00:23:12.040
No. it's called
playing hard to get back.

340
00:23:12.040 --> 00:23:14.520
SHE CHUCKLES
'Listen. just to tell you.

341
00:23:14.520 --> 00:23:16.320
'the guy at the forensics lab.

342
00:23:16.320 --> 00:23:18.960
'he's agreed to fast-track
Tina's handbag.'

343
00:23:18.960 --> 00:23:21.760
How fast is fast-track?
'They started looking today.

344
00:23:21.760 --> 00:23:23.680
'They should have it
in the next couple of days.

345
00:23:25.120 --> 00:23:28.520
'So. can we have
that drink tomorrow?'

346
00:23:28.520 --> 00:23:30.240
The Italian?
'Again?'

347
00:23:30.240 --> 00:23:32.480
Yeah. well. the Italian's
our new thing. isn't it?

348
00:23:32.480 --> 00:23:35.160
'In that case. how's six?'

349
00:23:35.160 --> 00:23:38.360
Yes. six I can do.
Now stop disturbing me.

350
00:23:38.360 --> 00:23:41.160
Some of us have got work to do.
I'll see you tomorrow.

351
00:23:44.480 --> 00:23:46.000
'That was not to do
with the affair.'

352
00:23:46.000 --> 00:23:49.720
'I apologise. I'm sorry.'
'I was angry.

353
00:23:49.720 --> 00:23:52.880
'And I did things that
I will never forgive myself for.'

354
00:24:00.440 --> 00:24:04.240
Like I said. we will make arrests
and continue to make arrests

355
00:24:04.240 --> 00:24:06.440
wherever we see it as helpful
to the investigation.

356
00:24:06.440 --> 00:24:08.120
These are two such examples.

357
00:24:08.120 --> 00:24:10.360
Is that not just
a scatter-gun approach?

358
00:24:10.360 --> 00:24:13.320
I'm not quite sure you can describe
two of anything as "scatter-gun".

359
00:24:13.320 --> 00:24:15.200
What they are is necessary.

360
00:24:15.200 --> 00:24:16.880
If they were both men in their 50s.

361
00:24:16.880 --> 00:24:19.000
would it be safe to say
they're parents at the school?

362
00:24:19.000 --> 00:24:21.400
I'm not going to comment.
But were they known to the victim?

363
00:24:21.400 --> 00:24:22.800
I'm not going to comment either.

364
00:24:22.800 --> 00:24:25.000
But conversations have moved
the inquiry forward.

365
00:24:25.000 --> 00:24:26.280
How have they moved the...?

366
00:24:26.280 --> 00:24:28.720
And both men... both men
have been released without charge.

367
00:24:28.720 --> 00:24:31.400
ALL CLAMOUR
That is all. Thank you.

368
00:24:31.400 --> 00:24:34.000
Are you looking at other suspects?
Detective!

369
00:24:34.000 --> 00:24:35.720
A few more questions.
Detective!

370
00:24:38.360 --> 00:24:39.840
REPORTER: 'Police fending off

371
00:24:39.840 --> 00:24:42.800
'a seemingly endless list
of questions this morning...'

372
00:24:42.800 --> 00:24:45.000
'What they are is necessary.'

373
00:24:45.000 --> 00:24:49.760
'..anger at what many people deem
to be a distinct lack of progress.'

374
00:24:49.760 --> 00:24:51.240
'But were they known to the victim?'

375
00:24:51.240 --> 00:24:53.240
'I'm not going to comment
on that either. but...'

376
00:24:53.240 --> 00:24:55.480
I don't know what's worse...

377
00:24:55.480 --> 00:24:58.520
whether he was known to her
or a stranger.

378
00:25:05.440 --> 00:25:06.680
SHE SIGHS

379
00:25:09.160 --> 00:25:10.520
SIGHS

380
00:25:20.000 --> 00:25:21.160
You exercise.

381
00:25:22.280 --> 00:25:24.520
So?
So spare me the dirty look.

382
00:25:26.880 --> 00:25:28.560
You're the one with the dirty look.

383
00:25:56.840 --> 00:25:59.680
Charlie-X-ray-655.
suspect moving off. over.

384
00:26:00.840 --> 00:26:02.280
The police are still watching...

385
00:26:03.520 --> 00:26:04.840
..in case you didn't know.

386
00:26:04.840 --> 00:26:07.120
They're not hiding the fact. Dylan.

387
00:26:07.120 --> 00:26:09.280
They want us to know
they're interested in your dad.

388
00:26:10.560 --> 00:26:12.240
As if we need fucking reminding.

389
00:26:15.160 --> 00:26:16.560
SHE SIGHS

390
00:26:18.160 --> 00:26:19.400
Sorry.

391
00:26:23.800 --> 00:26:26.880
He wants me to go to the police
and tell them the times he was here.

392
00:26:26.880 --> 00:26:29.200
You better not be helping him.

393
00:26:29.200 --> 00:26:32.200
I've seen him acting all nice
and shit. I know what he's up to.

394
00:26:32.200 --> 00:26:35.760
They wouldn't have just arrested
him. not without a reason.

395
00:26:39.480 --> 00:26:41.360
Get your stuff.
I'll take you to training.

396
00:27:08.120 --> 00:27:09.320
Come on. Michael.

397
00:27:10.600 --> 00:27:11.720
Talk to me.

398
00:27:22.320 --> 00:27:24.160
You've arrested Stephen Sedgwick?

399
00:27:25.600 --> 00:27:27.320
"Two men arrested."

400
00:27:27.320 --> 00:27:29.480
I was one of them.
I presume he's the other one.

401
00:27:30.760 --> 00:27:33.240
I can't tell you that.
"A man in his 50s."

402
00:27:33.240 --> 00:27:35.600
You know I can't tell you that.
But you've let him go?

403
00:27:38.080 --> 00:27:41.160
The other man who was arrested has
been released without charge. yes.

404
00:27:41.160 --> 00:27:43.240
Is that because you don't think
he was responsible.

405
00:27:43.240 --> 00:27:45.520
or you do think he was responsible
but you can't prove it?

406
00:27:45.520 --> 00:27:47.360
And has he denied it.
this other man?

407
00:27:47.360 --> 00:27:49.880
Denied?
Strangling my wife.

408
00:27:52.920 --> 00:27:55.480
And did he blame me?
Who told you she was strangled?

409
00:27:55.480 --> 00:27:56.920
I bet he did.
Answer that question.

410
00:27:56.920 --> 00:28:00.520
I would've done that if I was him.
Who told you she was strangled?

411
00:28:01.720 --> 00:28:02.880
SIGHS

412
00:28:06.840 --> 00:28:08.440
SIGHS

413
00:28:11.800 --> 00:28:12.960
I'm sorry.

414
00:28:22.080 --> 00:28:25.480
Alana hasn't gone
to her grandparents' to help them.

415
00:28:28.760 --> 00:28:30.680
She's gone to get away from me.

416
00:28:40.680 --> 00:28:42.360
Sarah's death is my fault.

417
00:28:48.640 --> 00:28:50.680
Michael. whatever it is
you need to say...

418
00:28:52.560 --> 00:28:53.840
..say it.

419
00:28:55.200 --> 00:28:59.320
It's just you and I. Michael.
It's just between you and I.

420
00:29:04.200 --> 00:29:06.280
I wasn't the husband she deserved.

421
00:29:06.280 --> 00:29:08.080
Well. maybe at first.

422
00:29:08.080 --> 00:29:10.280
but it hadn't been working
for a long time.

423
00:29:10.280 --> 00:29:13.520
so she found someone else.
someone who could...

424
00:29:15.200 --> 00:29:17.240
..give her what she needed.

425
00:29:19.040 --> 00:29:21.040
I'm sure she didn't think of it
like that.

426
00:29:21.040 --> 00:29:23.800
The affair was my fault.
How was it your fault?

427
00:29:26.120 --> 00:29:29.200
Well. she went to him.
Yeah. that's what I mean.

428
00:29:29.200 --> 00:29:32.880
Because... I wasn't enough.
It wasn't working.

429
00:29:32.880 --> 00:29:34.320
I wasn't what she needed.

430
00:29:34.320 --> 00:29:36.240
But she cheated on you.

431
00:29:36.240 --> 00:29:37.920
Yeah.
That's her fault.

432
00:29:37.920 --> 00:29:39.920
Michael. you can't go
blaming yourself for that.

433
00:29:39.920 --> 00:29:41.720
not when someone cheats.

434
00:29:58.920 --> 00:30:02.200
She went looking
for what she didn't have.

435
00:30:02.200 --> 00:30:04.280
Michael...
The affair was my fault.

436
00:30:06.160 --> 00:30:10.080
The affair. that was just a symptom.
We mustn't see it like that.

437
00:30:10.080 --> 00:30:11.920
Because that's what affairs
always are.

438
00:30:13.800 --> 00:30:18.120
And I... I couldn't confront her
about it. even though I knew.

439
00:30:19.680 --> 00:30:21.200
What do you mean. Michael?

440
00:30:21.200 --> 00:30:25.120
Because confronting sets things
in motion.

441
00:30:26.320 --> 00:30:28.760
You have to talk
about why it happened.

442
00:30:28.760 --> 00:30:34.160
and that causes fights and divorce
and damages reputations.

443
00:30:34.160 --> 00:30:36.000
and it all comes out.

444
00:30:37.400 --> 00:30:38.680
And I couldn't...

445
00:30:40.400 --> 00:30:42.600
..I couldn't do that
because I was ashamed.

446
00:30:44.080 --> 00:30:45.960
And I'll never forgive myself
for that.

447
00:30:48.440 --> 00:30:50.320
You look on that CCTV.

448
00:30:50.320 --> 00:30:52.840
do you see a man who's gonna fight
for his wife?

449
00:30:52.840 --> 00:30:55.200
Hm? You see a man who wants to.
but...

450
00:30:59.400 --> 00:31:02.000
..in the end. he just walks away
and gets into his car.

451
00:31:38.400 --> 00:31:40.840
The pathologist at the mortuary...

452
00:31:42.440 --> 00:31:44.760
..when I asked about the marks
on Sarah's neck.

453
00:31:44.760 --> 00:31:47.040
they said they thought
she'd been strangled.

454
00:31:49.120 --> 00:31:50.680
So that's how I knew.

455
00:31:58.280 --> 00:32:00.840
Er. yeah. no problem. follow me.
Thank you.

456
00:32:00.840 --> 00:32:03.280
Just right there for you. sir.
I'll just grab you some menus.

457
00:32:03.280 --> 00:32:05.400
That's great. thank you.
Be back in a second. Cheers.

458
00:32:11.080 --> 00:32:13.200
Hey. babe. It's me.

459
00:32:13.200 --> 00:32:16.080
Er. just ringing to say
I got our usual table.

460
00:32:16.080 --> 00:32:18.760
so hopefully.
I will see you shortly.

461
00:32:21.920 --> 00:32:23.920
There we go. sir.
Thank you.

462
00:32:23.920 --> 00:32:25.560
Did you want me to give you
a few minutes.

463
00:32:25.560 --> 00:32:27.720
pop back when she's arrived?

464
00:32:27.720 --> 00:32:30.880
I would love you to pop back
in a few minutes.

465
00:32:30.880 --> 00:32:32.200
OK. no problem.

466
00:32:32.200 --> 00:32:33.840
OK. I'll give you a second
to have a look.

467
00:32:40.280 --> 00:32:41.600
CLEARS THROAT

468
00:32:43.160 --> 00:32:48.360
We are far less convinced
that Sarah Polly was in Wales...

469
00:32:48.360 --> 00:32:50.200
PHONE BUZZES
..on the day she went missing.

470
00:32:50.200 --> 00:32:53.560
Stephen Sedgwick. we know.
was in possession of her debit card.

471
00:32:53.560 --> 00:32:56.560
CCTV on the bridge
shows he drove to Wales alone.

472
00:32:56.560 --> 00:33:01.120
No sign of anyone else in the car
on the way there or the way back.

473
00:33:01.120 --> 00:33:03.240
We're checking ANPR again

474
00:33:03.240 --> 00:33:06.440
and more CCTV and Ring doorbells
to close the gaps on his timeline

475
00:33:06.440 --> 00:33:08.040
across those three days.

476
00:33:08.040 --> 00:33:10.160
So we're eliminating him?
Not quite.

477
00:33:10.160 --> 00:33:12.960
He still needs an alibi for
some of the evenings of that week.

478
00:33:12.960 --> 00:33:16.960
And as we know. Michael Polly
still has some gaps in his timeline.

479
00:33:16.960 --> 00:33:20.360
Annie. if you could ask him
for those direct.

480
00:33:20.360 --> 00:33:24.280
Becky. if you could speak to Alana
and get her to corroborate. please.

481
00:33:24.280 --> 00:33:26.320
As for the comps
with other murders...

482
00:33:26.320 --> 00:33:27.360
SHE MOUTHS

483
00:33:27.360 --> 00:33:29.400
..I want everyone to be familiar
with the details

484
00:33:29.400 --> 00:33:30.560
so we can cross-reference.

485
00:33:30.560 --> 00:33:33.840
Until both men can account for
every second of those three days.

486
00:33:33.840 --> 00:33:34.960
we're not ruling them out.

487
00:33:34.960 --> 00:33:38.400
This is gonna be a late one. folks.
OK? Thank you.

488
00:33:38.400 --> 00:33:40.680
CHATTERING

